# 2026 SELF-EVALUATION

## WHAT YOU ACHIEVED

### 1. Reusable Idempotency Sidecar PoC

Developed a reusable idempotency sidecar PoC that could be integrated with different services through configuration. Evaluated the approach using Loan Setup, assessing retry behavior and the risk of duplicate operations while demonstrating minimal latency overhead under load.

### 2. Control Plane Integration and Cross-Team Contributions

Implemented Loan Setup's integration with Control Plane, including the configuration schema. Extended the work beyond our team's codebase by fixing a startup defect directly in Control Plane's configuration loader. The integration enabled configuration updates in DEV without redeploying Loan Setup.

### 3. SafePay Integration

Implemented Loan Setup changes to support updated SafePay API contracts across authorization, reversal, and funding flows. Updated request and response handling for transaction identifiers and installment plan details, and identified two API contract defects before release.

### 4. Platform Modernization and Reliability

Photon Lambda Migration — Migrated Pay-in-4 orchestration Lambda functions to Photon Lambda and deployed the changes to production, resolving issues during the transition.

Infrastructure Cost Optimization — Right-sized non-production Aurora resources and removed an unused replica to reduce infrastructure costs.

Gremlin Integration and Resiliency Testing — Integrated and configured Gremlin for resiliency testing, enabling CPU stress and latency fault-injection scenarios to evaluate application behavior under degraded conditions.

### 5. AI Agents and Shared Engineering Tools

Production Support Agent — Developed and delivered an agent now used by the team to automate GBP posting failure investigations and reporting. Replaced a nine-step manual process with a single-command workflow that collects and reconciles production data, identifies affected loans, and prepares reports for engineer review while preserving existing security controls.

QAC2 Validation Agent — Separately designed and built an end-to-end AI-driven validation workflow. Automated application login and loan creation through the UI, covered simulation testing, and integrated Log-lens to investigate failures and generate reports with root-cause analysis, impact assessments, team contacts, and recommended next steps. Completed the implementation and submitted it for review.

CCB Skills Contributions — Developed Snow Lite, AWS CLI, and Sophia SSH skills and contributed them to the shared CCB Skills library. Maintained the skills as underlying systems evolved. All three were subsequently used by other engineers in the development of Log-lens and RSA agents.

### 6. PVT Automation

Drove PVT automation to completion for post-deployment performance and acceptance testing. Identified automation opportunities, contributed to backlog planning, and worked with the platform team to address dependencies. Automated execution of performance and acceptance tests, as well as performance test reporting, reducing manual release-validation effort. Shared reusable approaches with other engineers.

